        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "25 Dun Emer Drive, Dundrum, Dublin 16\r\nFor Sale by Private Treaty\r\n\r\nOverview\r\nAdvised Minimum Value (AMV): €895,000\r\n\r\nProperty Type: Extended 4-Bed Semi-Detached House with Converted Attic & Self-Contained Granny Flat\r\n\r\nMain House Bedrooms: 4 Bedrooms + Converted Attic Space\r\n\r\nSelf-Contained Unit: Attached Side Granny Flat (Independent Entrance & Separated Garden Area)\r\n\r\nCondition: In Need of Refurbishment / Renovation Opportunity\r\n\r\nParking: Ample Off-Street Driveway (3–4 Vehicles)\r\n\r\nKW Team Castles are delighted to present 25 Dun Emer Drive to the Dublin 16 market — AMV €895,000.\r\n\r\nSituated in a mature and peaceful residential cul-de-sac off Sandyford Road, this substantial semi-detached property offers a rare combination of footprint, versatility, and location.\r\n\r\nBoasting an extended 4-bedroom main residence with a converted attic, alongside an attached self-contained side granny flat, this property presents a incredible project for buyers looking to create a substantial family home, cater for multi-generational living, or generate significant rental yield.\r\n\r\nProperty Description\r\nMain House Accommodation\r\nGround Floor: A welcoming entrance hall leads into a generous front reception room, flowing into a formal dining room and a functional kitchen area. To the rear sits a bright conservatory overlooking the main garden space.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor: Four well-proportioned bedrooms alongside a main family bathroom suite.\r\n\r\nAttic Conversion: A full staircase leads to a converted attic room, ideal as a dedicated home office, study, or hobby space.\r\n\r\nSelf-Contained Granny Flat\r\nPositioned to the side of the property with its own independent access, the self-contained unit offers excellent flexibility for extended family, a home business workspace, or rental income.\r\n\r\nGrounds & Exterior\r\nFront: Generous off-street parking driveway providing space for 3 to 4 cars.\r\n\r\nRear: The private rear garden has been thoughtfully divided between the main dwelling and the granny flat, providing independent outdoor spaces for both units.\r\n\r\nRenovation Opportunity\r\nWhile in need of cosmetic updating and modernization throughout, the property offers exceptional structural bones, an impressive overall floor area, and an ideal canvas to build substantial equity in a prime Dublin 16 location.\r\n\r\nKey Features\r\nAMV: €895,000\r\n\r\nPresented by: KW Team Castles\r\n\r\nSubstantial Footprint: 4 Bedrooms + Converted Attic Room\r\n\r\nSelf-Contained Side Unit: Ideal for multi-generational living or rental income\r\n\r\nDual Private Gardens: Rear garden separated for independent use\r\n\r\nConservatory: Sunroom addition to the rear of the main house\r\n\r\nGenerous Driveway: Off-street parking for 3–4 vehicles\r\n\r\nRefurbishment Opportunity: Blank canvas to modernize and add value\r\n\r\nPrime Location: Walking distance to Dundrum Town Centre & Luas\r\n\r\nLocation & Amenities\r\nDun Emer Drive is widely regarded as one of Dundrum's most convenient residential locations:\r\n\r\nTransport: Walking distance to the Balally and Dundrum Luas Green Line stops, providing access to St. Stephen’s Green in ~15 minutes. Minutes from the M50 motorway (Junction 13).\r\n\r\nShopping & Leisure: Steps away from Dundrum Town Centre, offering premier shopping, cinemas, restaurants, and cafes, alongside Airfield Estate and Ballawley Park.\r\n\r\nSchools: Surrounded by top-tier schools including Wesley College, Mount Anville, Taney National School, Notre Dame, and St. Attracta’s.\r\n\r\nViewing Details\r\nStrictly by private appointment with KW Team Castles. Early viewing is highly advised to explore the scope and potential on offer.\r\n\r\nBER: 107463614"
